{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Global text search over the store. query is ONE case-insensitive substring (spaces included). Searches control names/descs, every text facet (html, css, js, memory, ...), command text (name, desc, imports, parameter names, source) and text assets, across every library or scoped by lib / ctl / kinds (comma-separated subset of control,facet,command,asset; \"\" = all). Each library's flat index (runtime/dev/search/<lib>.idx, built on demand when missing) rules out records by trigram mask; every surviving candidate is then VERIFIED against the live record, so a hit is always true. FRESHNESS: each index remembers the files it was built from (record files, their attachment siblings, assets) with a fingerprint of their mtimes and sizes; before a library is searched those files are re-statted (no record is read; at most once per 2 s per library per process) and the library is rebuilt when anything moved (counted in indexes_built), so edits by any writer - dev.code commands, git, another process - are found by the next query, at worst 2 s late. Each hit is filtered by the session's read access to its record (security check_auth, as app.app.read; assets are public like app.app.asset). Returns FLAT {status, query, count (total), truncated, pruned_by_mask (false for queries under 3 bytes: full read), libraries_searched, libraries_ruled_out, indexes_built, candidates, denied, ms, matches:[{lib, kind, ctl, name, cmd|facet|asset, line (first matching line), preview (up to 3 matching lines), changed_since_index}]}.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse crate::dev::search::index::search;\n","params":[{"desc":"Library to search; \"\" or \"*\" = every library.","name":"lib","type":"String"},{"desc":"Control to search within; \"\" or \"*\" = every control. Naming a control excludes assets, which belong to the library.","name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"desc":"Comma-separated subset of control,facet,command,asset; \"\" = all four.","name":"kinds","type":"String"},{"desc":"One case-insensitive substring, spaces included (not a word list). Under 3 bytes it cannot use the masks and every record is read.","name":"query","type":"String"},{"desc":"Maximum matches returned (count still reports the total); <=0 means 50.","name":"limit","type":"Integer"},{"desc":"Request metadata filled in by the framework; every hit is filtered by this session's read access to the record.","name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"rmyhtz1a1d062caa1m4","readers":[],"time":1794498795759,"username":"system","writers":[]}